/-!
# The fibre criterion for relative effective Cartier divisors

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be flat with `X` locally noetherian, and let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose
closed subscheme `D` is flat over `S`. This file proves that `D` is a relative effective Cartier
divisor as soon as each of its fibres `D_s ⊆ X_s = X ×_S Spec κ(s)` over the residue fields of
`S` is an effective Cartier divisor
(`Scheme.IdealSheafData.isEffectiveCartier_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι`). With the
converse `Scheme.IdealSheafData.IsRelativeEffectiveCartier.isEffectiveCartier_comap_of_field`,
this characterizes relative effective Cartier divisors by their residue-field fibres
(`Scheme.IdealSheafData.isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι`).
The base `S` need not be noetherian; when it is locally noetherian and `f` is locally of finite
type, `X` is locally noetherian by Mathlib's `LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian`. The
criterion reduces the effective Cartier condition for a family over a general base to the same
condition for schemes over fields.

The fibre over any field-valued point `Spec K ⟶ S` is the base change of the fibre over the
residue field `κ(s)` of its image along the flat surjective morphism `Spec K ⟶ Spec κ(s)`. So the
fibre over `κ(s)` is effective Cartier exactly when the fibre over `K` is
(`Scheme.IdealSheafData.IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fst_of_comap_fiberι`, and
`Scheme.IdealSheafData.IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fiberι_of_comap_fst` when the fibre over `κ(s)`
is locally noetherian, by descent along flat surjective morphisms). The fibres over residue fields
of a locally noetherian `X` are locally noetherian
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isLocallyNoetherian_fiber`), so relative effective Cartier
divisors are also characterized by their geometric fibres
(`isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_of_isAlgClosed`).

The proof of the residue-field criterion works at a point `x` of `X` over `s`. For affine opens
`U ∋ x` and `W ∋ s` with `f(U) ⊆ W`, write `A = Γ(S, W)`, `B = Γ(X, U)`, `p` and `q` for the
primes of `s` and `x`, and `J = I(U)`. The scheme `Spec (κ(p) ⊗[A] B)` is an open subscheme of the
fibre over `Spec κ(p) ⟶ S`, so the ideal `J` generates in `(κ(p) ⊗[A] B)_Q`, for the prime `Q`
over `q`, an ideal generated by a nonzerodivisor. By the local criterion
`Module.Flat.exists_isSMulRegular_and_map_eq_span_singleton_iff_fiber` the same holds for `J B_q`,
that is, in the stalk `𝒪_{X,x}`, and on a locally noetherian scheme this makes `I` an effective
Cartier divisor near `x`
(`Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_eq_span_singleton_of_map_germ_eq_span_singleton`).

The criterion is pointwise: `I` is generated by a nonzerodivisor near a point `x` as soon as the
fibre of `I` over `f x` is an effective Cartier divisor
(`Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_eq_span_singleton_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι`). This gives
the criterion for families over an arbitrary base `T` that are base changes `X ×_S T` of a flat
family `X ⟶ S` with `X` locally noetherian, which is the form used after spreading out a family of
finite presentation to a noetherian base: the pullback of `I` is a relative effective Cartier
divisor over `T` exactly when its fibres over the points of `T` are effective Cartier divisors
(`isRelativeEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι`,
and its geometric-point form). Neither `T` nor `X ×_S T` need be locally noetherian. The fibre of
the base change over `t` is the base change of the fibre of `I` over `g t` along the field
extension `κ(g t) → κ(t)` (`Scheme.IdealSheafData.isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_comp_iff`), so it
is effective Cartier exactly when that fibre is; the noetherian criterion then makes `I` an
effective Cartier divisor near the image in `X` of each point of `X ×_S T`, and relative effective
Cartier divisors are stable under base change.

Over an arbitrary base, the criterion holds for smooth families: if `f : X ⟶ S` is smooth and the
closed subscheme of `I` is locally of finite presentation and flat over `S`, then `I` is a relative
effective Cartier divisor exactly when its fibres over the residue fields (or over the geometric
points) of `S` are effective Cartier divisors
(`isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι_of_smooth`). Here neither
`S` nor `X` need be locally noetherian. Near a point `x` over `s`, a generator `t ∈ I(U)` of the
fibre of `I` at `x` generates `I` on a basic open neighbourhood of `x`, by Nakayama's lemma and
finite presentation (`Module.Flat.exists_mem_and_map_eq_span_singleton_of_fiber`). The fibres of
`I` over all points of `S` make `t` a nonzerodivisor on each fibre ring of that neighbourhood, and
for a smooth algebra this makes `t` a nonzerodivisor
(`Algebra.Smooth.isSMulRegular_of_forall_isSMulRegular_fiber`, proved through a noetherian model).

## Main results

* `Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_eq_span_singleton_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι`: the
  pointwise criterion, giving a nonzerodivisor equation near every point over which the fibre is
  an effective Cartier divisor.
* `Scheme.IdealSheafData.isEffectiveCartier_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι`: an ideal sheaf
  whose closed subscheme is flat over the base, and whose residue-field fibres are effective
  Cartier divisors, is an effective Cartier divisor.
* `Scheme.IdealSheafData.isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι`:
  the fibre criterion for relative effective Cartier divisors over residue fields.
* `isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_of_isAlgClosed`: the fibre
  criterion for relative effective Cartier divisors over geometric points.
* `Scheme.IdealSheafData.isRelativeEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι`:
  the base change to `X ×_S T` of a divisor on a locally noetherian family `X ⟶ S` is a relative
  effective Cartier divisor as soon as its fibres over the image of `T` are effective Cartier.
* `isRelativeEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι`
  and `isRelativeEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_of_isAlgClosed`:
  the fibre criterion over residue fields and over geometric points for such base changes.
* `isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι_of_smooth` and
  `isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_of_isAlgClosed_of_smooth`:
  the fibre criterion over residue fields and over geometric points for a smooth family over an
  arbitrary base.
* `Scheme.IdealSheafData.IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fst_of_comap_fiberι`: effective Cartier
  residue-field fibres give effective Cartier fibres over every field-valued point.
* `Scheme.IdealSheafData.IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fiberι_of_comap_fst`: conversely, an effective
  Cartier fibre over a field-valued point gives an effective Cartier fibre over the residue field
  of its image, when the latter fibre is locally noetherian.

## References

* The Stacks Project, *Divisors*, Section *Relative effective Cartier divisors*: the fibrewise
  criterion for a closed subscheme flat over the base to be a relative effective Cartier divisor.
* N. M. Katz and B. Mazur, *Arithmetic Moduli of Elliptic Curves*, §1.2.
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData

variable {S T X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **Fibres over fields.** If the fibre of an ideal sheaf `I` on `X` over the residue field of
the image of the closed point of `Spec K` is an effective Cartier divisor, then so is the fibre of
`I` over the field-valued point `g : Spec K ⟶ S`. -/
theorem IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fst_of_comap_fiberι {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S}
    {K : Type u} [Field K] (g : Spec (.of K) ⟶ S)
    (h : (I.comap (f.fiberι (g (IsLocalRing.closedPoint K)))).IsEffectiveCartier) :
    (I.comap (pullback.fst f g)).IsEffectiveCartier := by
  rw [← descResidueField_stalkClosedPointTo_fromSpecResidueField K S g,
    isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_comp_iff]
  -- `Spec K ⟶ Spec κ(s)` is flat, as is every morphism to the spectrum of a field, and so is its
  -- base change. The fibre `f.fiber s` is the pullback of `f` along `S.fromSpecResidueField s`,
  -- with projections `f.fiberι s` and `f.fiberToSpecResidueField s`.
  exact h.comap (pullback.fst (f.fiberToSpecResidueField _) _)

/-- **Descent from fibres over fields.** If the fibre of an ideal sheaf `I` on `X` over the
field-valued point `g : Spec K ⟶ S` is an effective Cartier divisor, then so is its fibre over the
residue field of the image `s` of `g`, provided the fibre of `X` over `κ(s)` is locally
noetherian. -/
theorem IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fiberι_of_comap_fst {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S}
    {K : Type u} [Field K] (g : Spec (.of K) ⟶ S)
    [IsLocallyNoetherian (f.fiber (g (IsLocalRing.closedPoint K)))]
    (h : (I.comap (pullback.fst f g)).IsEffectiveCartier) :
    (I.comap (f.fiberι (g (IsLocalRing.closedPoint K)))).IsEffectiveCartier := by
  rw [← descResidueField_stalkClosedPointTo_fromSpecResidueField K S g,
    isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_comp_iff] at h
  -- `Spec K ⟶ Spec κ(s)` is flat and surjective, so its base change to the fibre over `κ(s)` is.
  have : Surjective (Spec.map (S.descResidueField (S.stalkClosedPointTo g))) :=
    ⟨fun _ ↦ ⟨default, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩⟩
  exact IsEffectiveCartier.of_comap (X := f.fiber _)
    (pullback.fst (f.fiberToSpecResidueField _) _) h

open Algebra.TensorProduct in
/-- Let `U ⊆ X` and `W ⊆ S` be affine opens with `f(U) ⊆ W`, so that `B = Γ(X, U)` is an algebra
over `A = Γ(S, W)`, and let `P` be a prime of `A`. If the fibre of `I` over the field-valued point
`Spec κ(P) ⟶ Spec A ⟶ S` is an effective Cartier divisor, then on the chart
`Spec (κ(P) ⊗[A] B)` of that fibre the ideal `I(U)` generates, in the local ring at every prime
`Q`, a principal ideal with a nonzerodivisor generator. -/
private theorem IsEffectiveCartier.exists_map_fiber_eq_span_singleton {I : X.IdealSheafData}
    {f : X ⟶ S} {W : S.Opens} (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (U : X.affineOpens) (hUW : U.1 ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ W)
    [Algebra Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U)] (hφ : f.appLE W U hUW = CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap _ _))
    (P : Ideal Γ(S, W)) [P.IsPrime]
    (h : (I.comap (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (algebraMap Γ(S, W) P.ResidueField)) ≫ hW.fromSpec))).IsEffectiveCartier)
    (Q : Ideal (P.Fiber Γ(X, U))) [Q.IsPrime] :
    ∃ g : Localization.AtPrime Q, IsSMulRegular (Localization.AtPrime Q) g ∧
      ((I.ideal U).map (includeRight : Γ(X, U) →ₐ[Γ(S, W)] P.Fiber Γ(X, U))).map
        (algebraMap (P.Fiber Γ(X, U)) (Localization.AtPrime Q)) = Ideal.span {g} := by
  -- The chart: `Spec (κ(P) ⊗[A] B) ≅ Spec κ(P) ×_{Spec A} Spec B` is an open subscheme of the
  -- fibre `X ×_S Spec κ(P)`.
  have hU : IsAffineOpen U.1 := U.2
  have e₁ : Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U))) ≫ hW.fromSpec =
      hU.fromSpec ≫ f := hφ ▸ IsAffineOpen.SpecMap_appLE_fromSpec f hW hU hUW
  let m := pullback.map _ (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, W) P.ResidueField))) f _
    hU.fromSpec (𝟙 _) hW.fromSpec e₁ (Category.id_comp _).symm
  have : IsOpenImmersion m := Scheme.pullback_map_isOpenImmersion _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _
  let c := (pullbackSpecIso Γ(S, W) P.ResidueField Γ(X, U)).inv ≫ (pullbackSymmetry _ _).hom ≫ m
  have hc : c ≫ pullback.fst _ _ =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom includeRight.toRingHom) ≫ hU.fromSpec := by
    simp [c, m]
  have hI := h.comap c
  rw [← comap_comp, hc, comap_comp, comap_fromSpec_eq_ofIdealTop,
    comap_ofIdealTop_map_ΓSpecIso_inv] at hI
  exact hI.exists_map_algebraMap_eq_span_singleton Q

open Algebra.TensorProduct in
/-- **The pointwise fibre criterion.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be flat with `X` locally noetherian, and
let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed subscheme is flat over `S`. If the fibre of `I` over
the residue field of `f x` is an effective Cartier divisor, then `I` is generated by a
nonzerodivisor on an affine open neighbourhood of `x`. -/
theorem exists_eq_span_singleton_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S} [Flat f] [Flat (I.subschemeι ≫ f)] {x : X}
    (h : (I.comap (f.fiberι (f x))).IsEffectiveCartier) :
    ∃ U : X.affineOpens, x ∈ U.1 ∧
      ∃ a : Γ(X, U), IsSMulRegular Γ(X, U) a ∧ I.ideal U = Ideal.span {a} := by
  -- Affine opens `W ∋ f x` of `S` and `U ∋ x` of `X` with `f(U) ⊆ W`, and `B = Γ(X, U)` as an
  -- algebra over `A = Γ(S, W)`.
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨W, hW, rfl⟩, hxW, -⟩ :=
    S.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ (f x)) isOpen_univ
  replace hW : IsAffineOpen W := hW
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨U, hU, rfl⟩, hxU, hUW⟩ := X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
    (f.mem_preimage.mpr hxW) (f ⁻¹ᵁ W).isOpen
  replace hU : IsAffineOpen U := hU
  let _ : Algebra Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U) := (f.appLE W U hUW).hom.toAlgebra
  have : IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian ⟨U, hU⟩
  have : Module.Flat Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U) := f.flat_appLE hW hU hUW
  have : Module.Flat Γ(S, W) (Γ(X, U) ⧸ I.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩) := by
    rw [← RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U),
      Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]
    exact I.flat_appLE_comp_ofHom_quotient_mk f hW ⟨U, hU⟩ hUW
  -- The prime `q` of `x` in `B` lies over the prime `p` of `f x` in `A`; choose the prime `Q` of
  -- the fibre ring `κ(p) ⊗[A] B` over `q`.
  let p := hW.primeIdealOf ⟨f x, hxW⟩
  let q := hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩
  have hqp : PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U)) q = p :=
    IsAffineOpen.comap_primeIdealOf_appLE W hW U hU hUW hxU
  let Q := PrimeSpectrum.preimageEquivFiber Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U) p ⟨q, hqp⟩
  have hQ : Q.asIdeal.comap includeRight = q.asIdeal := by
    have := congrArg Subtype.val
      ((PrimeSpectrum.preimageEquivFiber Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U) p).symm_apply_apply ⟨q, hqp⟩)
    rwa [PrimeSpectrum.preimageEquivFiber_symm_apply_coe, PrimeSpectrum.ext_iff,
      PrimeSpectrum.comap_asIdeal] at this
  -- The field-valued point `Spec κ(p) ⟶ Spec A ⟶ S` lies over `f x`.
  have hp : (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, W) p.asIdeal.ResidueField)) ≫
      hW.fromSpec) (IsLocalRing.closedPoint p.asIdeal.ResidueField) = f x :=
    (Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ _).trans <| (congrArg hW.fromSpec
      (Spec.map_algebraMap_residueField_closedPoint p)).trans (hW.fromSpec_primeIdealOf _)
  -- The fibre of `I` over `Spec κ(p) ⟶ S` is effective Cartier, so `I(U)` generates a principal
  -- ideal, with a nonzerodivisor generator, in the local ring of the fibre ring at `Q`, hence
  -- also in `B_q`.
  obtain ⟨b, hb, hIb⟩ := (Module.Flat.exists_isSMulRegular_and_map_eq_span_singleton_iff_fiber
    p.asIdeal (I.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩) Q.asIdeal).mpr
      (IsEffectiveCartier.exists_map_fiber_eq_span_singleton hW ⟨U, hU⟩ hUW rfl p.asIdeal
        (IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fst_of_comap_fiberι _ (hp ▸ h)) Q.asIdeal)
  -- Transport to the stalk `𝒪_{X,x}`, the localization of `B` at `q`, and spread the equation of
  -- the stalk to an affine open neighbourhood of `x`.
  obtain ⟨a, ha, hIa⟩ :=
    X.exists_map_germ_eq_span_singleton_of_localizationAtPrime ⟨U, hU⟩ hxU _ hQ hb hIb
  exact exists_eq_span_singleton_of_map_germ_eq_span_singleton ⟨U, hU⟩ hxU ha hIa

/-- **The fibre criterion for effective Cartier divisors.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be flat with `X`
locally noetherian, and let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed subscheme is flat over `S`.
If the fibre of `I` over the residue field of every point of `S` is an effective Cartier divisor,
then `I` is an effective Cartier divisor. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartier_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S} [Flat f] [Flat (I.subschemeι ≫ f)]
    (h : ∀ s : S, (I.comap (f.fiberι s)).IsEffectiveCartier) : I.IsEffectiveCartier :=
  (isEffectiveCartier_iff I).mpr fun x ↦
    exists_eq_span_singleton_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι (h (f x))

/-- **The fibre criterion for relative effective Cartier divisors over residue fields.** Let
`f : X ⟶ S` be flat with `X` locally noetherian, and let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed
subscheme is flat over `S`. Then `I` is a relative effective Cartier divisor if and only if its
fibre over the residue field of every point of `S` is an effective Cartier divisor. -/
theorem isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S} [Flat f]
    [Flat (I.subschemeι ≫ f)] :
    I.IsRelativeEffectiveCartier f ↔ ∀ s : S, (I.comap (f.fiberι s)).IsEffectiveCartier :=
  ⟨fun hI s ↦ hI.isEffectiveCartier_comap_of_field (S.fromSpecResidueField s), fun h ↦
    (isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff I f).mpr
      ⟨isEffectiveCartier_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι h, inferInstance⟩⟩

/-- **The fibre criterion for relative effective Cartier divisors over geometric points.** Let
`f : X ⟶ S` be flat with `X` locally noetherian, and let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed
subscheme is flat over `S`. Then `I` is a relative effective Cartier divisor if and only if its
fibre over every geometric point `Spec K ⟶ S`, with `K` algebraically closed, is an effective
Cartier divisor. -/
theorem isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_of_isAlgClosed
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S} [Flat f]
    [Flat (I.subschemeι ≫ f)] :
    I.IsRelativeEffectiveCartier f ↔ ∀ (K : Type u) [Field K] [IsAlgClosed K]
      (g : Spec (.of K) ⟶ S), (I.comap (pullback.fst f g)).IsEffectiveCartier := by
  refine ⟨fun hI K _ _ g ↦ hI.isEffectiveCartier_comap_of_field g, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι]
  intro s
  -- The fibre of `f` over `κ(s)` is locally noetherian since `X` is
  -- (`Scheme.Hom.isLocallyNoetherian_fiber`).
  have hs := IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fiberι_of_comap_fst (S.fromSpecAlgebraicClosure s) (h _ _)
  -- The geometric point over `s` maps to `s`.
  convert hs using 3 <;> exact (S.fromSpecAlgebraicClosure_apply s _).symm

/-- **The fibre criterion after base change from a noetherian family.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be flat
with `X` locally noetherian, let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed subscheme is flat over
`S`, and let `g : T ⟶ S` be any morphism. If the fibre of `I` over the residue field of `g t` is
an effective Cartier divisor for every point `t` of `T`, then the pullback of `I` to `X ×_S T` is
a relative effective Cartier divisor over `T`. Neither `T` nor `X ×_S T` need be locally
noetherian, and nothing is assumed about the fibres of `I` over points outside the image of `g`.
-/
theorem isRelativeEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S} [Flat f]
    [Flat (I.subschemeι ≫ f)] (g : T ⟶ S)
    (h : ∀ t : T, (I.comap (f.fiberι (g t))).IsEffectiveCartier) :
    (I.comap (pullback.fst f g)).IsRelativeEffectiveCartier (pullback.snd f g) := by
  rw [IsRelativeEffectiveCartier.comap_iff]
  refine isEffectiveCartier_of_forall_exists_isOpenImmersion _ fun z ↦ ?_
  -- An affine open `U` of `X`, around the image of `z`, on which `I` has a nonzerodivisor
  -- equation `a`: the image of `z` in `S` is `g` of its image in `T`.
  obtain ⟨U, hzU, a, ha, hUa⟩ := exists_eq_span_singleton_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι
    (x := pullback.fst f g z) (by
      rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, pullback.condition, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply]
      exact h _)
  -- On `U`, the restriction of `I` is a relative effective Cartier divisor over `S`.
  have hU : (I.comap U.1.ι).IsRelativeEffectiveCartier (U.1.ι ≫ f) := by
    refine (isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff _ _).mpr ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · exact isEffectiveCartier_comap_ι_of_eq_span_singleton U ha hUa
    · -- The closed subscheme of the restriction is an open subscheme of that of `I`.
      rw [← comapIso_hom_fst, Category.assoc, pullback.condition_assoc]
      infer_instance
  -- Hence so is its pullback to `U ×_S T`, which is an open subscheme of `X ×_S T` containing `z`.
  let φ := pullback.map (U.1.ι ≫ f) g f g U.1.ι (𝟙 T) (𝟙 S) (by simp) (by simp)
  refine ⟨pullback (U.1.ι ≫ f) g, φ, inferInstance, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [Scheme.Pullback.range_map]
    exact ⟨by rwa [Set.mem_preimage, Scheme.Opens.range_ι], by simp⟩
  · have hφ : φ ≫ pullback.fst f g = pullback.fst (U.1.ι ≫ f) g ≫ U.1.ι := pullback.lift_fst _ _ _
    rw [← comap_comp, hφ, comap_comp]
    exact (hU.comap g).isEffectiveCartier

/-- **The fibre criterion over geometric points after base change from a noetherian family.** Let
`f : X ⟶ S` be flat with `X` locally noetherian, let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed
subscheme is flat over `S`, and let `g : T ⟶ S` be any morphism. Then the pullback of `I` to
`X ×_S T` is a relative effective Cartier divisor over `T` if and only if its fibre over every
geometric point `Spec K ⟶ T`, with `K` algebraically closed, is an effective Cartier divisor. -/
theorem isRelativeEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_of_isAlgClosed
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S} [Flat f]
    [Flat (I.subschemeι ≫ f)] (g : T ⟶ S) :
    (I.comap (pullback.fst f g)).IsRelativeEffectiveCartier (pullback.snd f g) ↔
      ∀ (K : Type u) [Field K] [IsAlgClosed K] (h : Spec (.of K) ⟶ T),
        ((I.comap (pullback.fst f g)).comap
          (pullback.fst (pullback.snd f g) h)).IsEffectiveCartier := by
  refine ⟨fun hI K _ _ h ↦ hI.isEffectiveCartier_comap_of_field h, fun H ↦ ?_⟩
  refine isRelativeEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι g fun t ↦ ?_
  -- The geometric point `Spec κ(t)ᵃˡᵍ ⟶ T ⟶ S` lies over `g t`, and the fibre of `f` over `κ(g t)`
  -- is locally noetherian (`Scheme.Hom.isLocallyNoetherian_fiber`).
  have ht := IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fiberι_of_comap_fst (T.fromSpecAlgebraicClosure t ≫ g)
    ((isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_comp_iff g _).mpr (H _ _))
  convert ht using 3 <;> exact ((Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ _).trans
    (congrArg g (T.fromSpecAlgebraicClosure_apply t _))).symm

/-- **The fibre criterion over residue fields after base change from a noetherian family.** Let
`f : X ⟶ S` be flat with `X` locally noetherian, let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed
subscheme is flat over `S`, and let `g : T ⟶ S` be any morphism. Then the pullback of `I` to
`X ×_S T` is a relative effective Cartier divisor over `T` if and only if its fibre over the
residue field of every point of `T` is an effective Cartier divisor. -/
theorem isRelativeEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S} [Flat f]
    [Flat (I.subschemeι ≫ f)] (g : T ⟶ S) :
    (I.comap (pullback.fst f g)).IsRelativeEffectiveCartier (pullback.snd f g) ↔
      ∀ t : T, ((I.comap (pullback.fst f g)).comap
        ((pullback.snd f g).fiberι t)).IsEffectiveCartier := by
  refine ⟨fun hI t ↦ hI.isEffectiveCartier_comap_of_field (T.fromSpecResidueField t), fun H ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [isRelativeEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_of_isAlgClosed]
  exact fun K _ _ h ↦ IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fst_of_comap_fiberι h (H _)

/-! ### Smooth families over an arbitrary base -/

open Algebra.TensorProduct in
/-- **Local generators from a fibre.** Let `f : X ⟶ S`, let `U ⊆ X` and `W ⊆ S` be affine opens
with `f(U) ⊆ W`, and let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed subscheme is flat over `S`
and with `I(U)` finitely generated. If the fibre of `I` over the residue field of `f x` is an
effective Cartier divisor for a point `x ∈ U`, then `I` is generated by one element on a basic
open neighbourhood of `x` in `U`. No noetherian hypothesis is needed. -/
private theorem exists_mem_basicOpen_and_ideal_eq_span_singleton {I : X.IdealSheafData}
    {f : X ⟶ S} [Flat (I.subschemeι ≫ f)] {W : S.Opens} (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (U : X.affineOpens)
    (hUW : U.1 ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ W) (hJ : (I.ideal U).FG) {x : X} (hxU : x ∈ U.1)
    (h : (I.comap (f.fiberι (f x))).IsEffectiveCartier) :
    ∃ r : Γ(X, U), x ∈ (X.affineBasicOpen r).1 ∧
      ∃ t, I.ideal (X.affineBasicOpen r) = Ideal.span {t} := by
  let _ : Algebra Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U) := (f.appLE W U hUW).hom.toAlgebra
  have : Module.Flat Γ(S, W) (Γ(X, U) ⧸ I.ideal U) := by
    rw [← RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U),
      Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]
    exact I.flat_appLE_comp_ofHom_quotient_mk f hW U hUW
  -- The prime `q` of `x` in `B = Γ(X, U)` lies over the prime `p` of `f x` in `A = Γ(S, W)`;
  -- choose the prime `Q` of the fibre ring `κ(p) ⊗[A] B` over `q`.
  have hxW : f x ∈ W := hUW hxU
  let p := hW.primeIdealOf ⟨f x, hxW⟩
  let q := U.2.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩
  have hqp : PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U)) q = p :=
    IsAffineOpen.comap_primeIdealOf_appLE W hW U.1 U.2 hUW hxU
  let Q := PrimeSpectrum.preimageEquivFiber Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U) p ⟨q, hqp⟩
  have hQ : Q.asIdeal.comap includeRight = q.asIdeal := by
    have := congrArg Subtype.val
      ((PrimeSpectrum.preimageEquivFiber Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U) p).symm_apply_apply ⟨q, hqp⟩)
    rwa [PrimeSpectrum.preimageEquivFiber_symm_apply_coe, PrimeSpectrum.ext_iff,
      PrimeSpectrum.comap_asIdeal] at this
  -- The field-valued point `Spec κ(p) ⟶ Spec A ⟶ S` lies over `f x`.
  have hp : (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, W) p.asIdeal.ResidueField)) ≫
      hW.fromSpec) (IsLocalRing.closedPoint p.asIdeal.ResidueField) = f x :=
    (Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ _).trans <| (congrArg hW.fromSpec
      (Spec.map_algebraMap_residueField_closedPoint p)).trans (hW.fromSpec_primeIdealOf _)
  -- `I(U)` generates a principal ideal in the local ring of the fibre ring at `Q`, so `I(U) B_q`
  -- is generated by an element `t` of `I(U)`, and `I(U)` is generated by `t` on some `D(r) ∋ x`.
  obtain ⟨g, -, hIg⟩ := IsEffectiveCartier.exists_map_fiber_eq_span_singleton hW U hUW rfl
    p.asIdeal (IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fst_of_comap_fiberι _ (hp ▸ h)) Q.asIdeal
  obtain ⟨t, htI, hIt⟩ :=
    Module.Flat.exists_mem_and_map_eq_span_singleton_of_fiber p.asIdeal hJ Q.asIdeal hIg
  obtain ⟨r, hrq, hrI⟩ := Ideal.exists_notMem_smul_le_span_singleton_of_map_le
    (P := Q.asIdeal.comap includeRight) _ hJ hIt.le
  rw [hQ] at hrq
  have := U.2.isLocalization_basicOpen r
  refine ⟨r, ?_, algebraMap Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen r) t, ?_⟩
  · let _ := TopCat.Presheaf.algebra_section_stalk X.presheaf ⟨x, hxU⟩
    have := U.2.isLocalization_stalk ⟨x, hxU⟩
    exact (X.mem_basicOpen r x hxU).mpr
      ((IsLocalization.AtPrime.isUnit_to_map_iff (X.presheaf.stalk x) _ r).mpr hrq)
  · rw [← I.map_ideal_basicOpen]
    exact Ideal.map_algebraMap_away_eq_span_singleton htI hrI

open Algebra.TensorProduct in
/-- Let `U ⊆ X` and `W ⊆ S` be affine opens with `f(U) ⊆ W`, so that `B = Γ(X, U)` is an algebra
over `A = Γ(S, W)`, and let `P` be a prime of `A`. If `I(U)` is generated by `a` and the fibre of
`I` over the field-valued point `Spec κ(P) ⟶ Spec A ⟶ S` is an effective Cartier divisor, then
`1 ⊗ a` is a nonzerodivisor on the fibre ring `κ(P) ⊗[A] B`. -/
private theorem IsEffectiveCartier.isSMulRegular_fiber_of_ideal_eq_span_singleton
    {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S} {W : S.Opens} (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (U : X.affineOpens)
    (hUW : U.1 ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ W) [Algebra Γ(S, W) Γ(X, U)]
    (hφ : f.appLE W U hUW = CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap _ _)) (P : Ideal Γ(S, W)) [P.IsPrime]
    (h : (I.comap (pullback.fst f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (algebraMap Γ(S, W) P.ResidueField)) ≫ hW.fromSpec))).IsEffectiveCartier)
    {a : Γ(X, U)} (hIa : I.ideal U = Ideal.span {a}) :
    IsSMulRegular (P.Fiber Γ(X, U)) ((1 : P.ResidueField) ⊗ₜ[Γ(S, W)] a) := by
  -- It suffices that every `y` killed by `1 ⊗ a` vanishes at every maximal ideal `Q`.
  refine .of_right_eq_zero_of_smul fun y hy ↦ ?_
  refine eq_zero_of_localization y fun Q hQ ↦ ?_
  -- In the local ring at `Q`, the image of `1 ⊗ a` generates the same ideal as a nonzerodivisor
  -- `g`, so it is a nonzerodivisor.
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hIg⟩ := IsEffectiveCartier.exists_map_fiber_eq_span_singleton hW U hUW hφ P h Q
  rw [hIa, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton,
    includeRight_apply] at hIg
  have hreg := hg.of_span_singleton_le hIg.symm.le
  -- So `y` vanishes at `Q`.
  refine hreg.right_eq_zero_of_smul ?_
  rw [smul_eq_mul, ← map_mul, ← smul_eq_mul, hy, map_zero]

/-- **The fibre criterion for effective Cartier divisors on a smooth family.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be
smooth, and let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed subscheme is locally of finite
presentation and flat over `S`. If the fibre of `I` over the residue field of every point of `S`
is an effective Cartier divisor, then `I` is an effective Cartier divisor. Neither `S` nor `X`
need be locally noetherian. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartier_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι_of_smooth {I : X.IdealSheafData}
    {f : X ⟶ S} [Smooth f] [Flat (I.subschemeι ≫ f)] [LocallyOfFinitePresentation I.subschemeι]
    (h : ∀ s : S, (I.comap (f.fiberι s)).IsEffectiveCartier) : I.IsEffectiveCartier := by
  refine (isEffectiveCartier_iff I).mpr fun x ↦ ?_
  -- Affine opens `W ∋ f x` of `S` and `U ∋ x` of `X` with `f(U) ⊆ W`.
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨W, hW, rfl⟩, hxW, -⟩ :=
    S.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ (f x)) isOpen_univ
  replace hW : IsAffineOpen W := hW
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨U, hU, rfl⟩, hxU, hUW⟩ := X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
    (f.mem_preimage.mpr hxW) (f ⁻¹ᵁ W).isOpen
  -- `I` is generated by one element `a` on a basic open `U' ∋ x` of `U`.
  obtain ⟨r, hxr, a, hIa⟩ := exists_mem_basicOpen_and_ideal_eq_span_singleton hW ⟨U, hU⟩ hUW
    (I.ker_subschemeι ▸
      IsClosedImmersion.locallyOfFinitePresentation_iff.mp ‹_› ⟨U, hU⟩) hxU (h (f x))
  refine ⟨X.affineBasicOpen r, hxr, a, ?_, hIa⟩
  -- `a` is a nonzerodivisor on each fibre ring of the smooth `Γ(S, W)`-algebra `Γ(X, U')`, hence
  -- on `Γ(X, U')`.
  have hU'W : (X.affineBasicOpen r).1 ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ W := (X.basicOpen_le r).trans hUW
  let _ : Algebra Γ(S, W) Γ(X, (X.affineBasicOpen r).1) := (f.appLE W _ hU'W).hom.toAlgebra
  have : Algebra.Smooth Γ(S, W) Γ(X, (X.affineBasicOpen r).1) :=
    HasRingHomProperty.appLE @Smooth f ‹_› ⟨W, hW⟩ (X.affineBasicOpen r) hU'W
  exact Algebra.Smooth.isSMulRegular_of_forall_isSMulRegular_fiber (R := Γ(S, W)) fun P _ ↦
    IsEffectiveCartier.isSMulRegular_fiber_of_ideal_eq_span_singleton hW (X.affineBasicOpen r)
      hU'W rfl P (IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fst_of_comap_fiberι _ (h _)) hIa

/-- **The fibre criterion for relative effective Cartier divisors on a smooth family.** Let
`f : X ⟶ S` be smooth, and let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed subscheme is locally of
finite presentation and flat over `S`. Then `I` is a relative effective Cartier divisor if and
only if its fibre over the residue field of every point of `S` is an effective Cartier divisor.
This is the form of the criterion over an arbitrary base: neither `S` nor `X` need be locally
noetherian. -/
theorem isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι_of_smooth
    {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S} [Smooth f] [Flat (I.subschemeι ≫ f)]
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation I.subschemeι] :
    I.IsRelativeEffectiveCartier f ↔ ∀ s : S, (I.comap (f.fiberι s)).IsEffectiveCartier :=
  ⟨fun hI s ↦ hI.isEffectiveCartier_comap_of_field (S.fromSpecResidueField s), fun h ↦
    (isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff I f).mpr
      ⟨isEffectiveCartier_of_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι_of_smooth h, inferInstance⟩⟩

/-- **The fibre criterion over geometric points for a smooth family.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be smooth,
and let `I` be an ideal sheaf on `X` whose closed subscheme is locally of finite presentation and
flat over `S`. Then `I` is a relative effective Cartier divisor if and only if its fibre over
every geometric point `Spec K ⟶ S`, with `K` algebraically closed, is an effective Cartier
divisor. -/
theorem isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fst_of_isAlgClosed_of_smooth
    {I : X.IdealSheafData} {f : X ⟶ S} [Smooth f] [Flat (I.subschemeι ≫ f)]
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation I.subschemeι] :
    I.IsRelativeEffectiveCartier f ↔ ∀ (K : Type u) [Field K] [IsAlgClosed K]
      (g : Spec (.of K) ⟶ S), (I.comap (pullback.fst f g)).IsEffectiveCartier := by
  refine ⟨fun hI K _ _ g ↦ hI.isEffectiveCartier_comap_of_field g, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [isRelativeEffectiveCartier_iff_forall_isEffectiveCartier_comap_fiberι_of_smooth]
  intro s
  -- The fibres of `f` are locally of finite type over fields, so locally noetherian.
  have (s' : S) : IsLocallyNoetherian (f.fiber s') :=
    have : LocallyOfFiniteType (pullback.snd f (S.fromSpecResidueField s')) := inferInstance
    @LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian _ _ (f.fiberToSpecResidueField s') this _
  have hs := IsEffectiveCartier.comap_fiberι_of_comap_fst (S.fromSpecAlgebraicClosure s) (h _ _)
  convert hs using 3 <;> exact (S.fromSpecAlgebraicClosure_apply s _).symm

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData
